      "info": {
        "title": "3ds-recorder",
        "author": "BolgarMaxym97",
        "description": "Record your whole Nintendo 3DS screen — games, HOME Menu and apps, both screens with sound — with a Luma3DS sysmodule. Converts recordings to MP4 on the console and sends them to your phone over Wi-Fi via QR code. Old & New 3DS.",
        "category": [
          "homebrew"
        ],
        "console": [
          "3DS"
        ],
        "version": "v1.5.0",
        "license": "MIT",
        "last_updated": "2026-11-19 at 15:13 (UTC)",
        "releasenotes": "v1.5.0 (2026-11-19)\n3DS Recorder now speaks ten languages, records faster on an Old 3DS, works next to HOME Menu battery mods, and can leave recordings unconverted until you download them.\n\nTested on an Old 3DS with Luma3DS 13.5 in Monster Hunter 4G, Smash Bros, Pokémon Ultra Moon, Kirby and Mario Kart 7. This release has not been tried on a New 3DS yet. If something goes wrong, please open an issue and attach the log (phone page → Log for the developer, or /3ds/recorder/app.log and recorder.log from the SD card).\n\nWhat's new since 1.4.0\n\n- Ten languages: English, Українська, Deutsch, Español, Français, Italiano, Português (Brazil), 日本語, 简体中文 and 繁體中文.\n  - The first run offers the console's own language.\n  - All languages fit on one screen in the language list.\n  - The phone page follows the app's language; the converter page for computers follows the browser's.\n  - Japanese and Chinese have their own fonts, loaded only while that language is on.\n- Fixed: battery percentage mods for HOME Menu showed \"Error\" while the recorder ran (#10). The notification LED now goes through the system's own LED service, so the recorder no longer keeps the console's MCU connection to itself.\n- Convert To MP4: Automatically or On Download (#16). With On Download the app leaves .r3d files alone and converts a recording only when you send it to a phone (Settings → App).\n- Bottom Screen FPS (#18). With both screens recorded, the bottom one can be captured at 15, 10, 5 or 1 fps, leaving more of an Old 3DS to the top s...\n\n----------\n\nv1.4.0 (2026-11-18)\nMonster Hunter 4G, X and XX now work on an Old 3DS, recordings run faster on an Old 3DS, and the console can convert with the lid closed. Recordings can also be converted to MP4 on a computer, on the converter page.\n\nTested on an Old 3DS with Luma3DS 13.5 in Monster Hunter 4G, Kirby, Smash Bros, Pokémon Ultra Moon and Mario Kart 7. The New 3DS changes have not been tried on a New 3DS yet. If something goes wrong, please open an issue and attach the log (phone page → Log for the developer, or /3ds/recorder/app.log and recorder.log from the SD card).\n\nWhat's new since 1.3.0\n\n- Fixed: Monster Hunter 4G, X and XX crashed on an Old 3DS seconds after they started (#7).\n  - These games need all of the console's extended memory, so the recorder no longer puts its helper plugin into them.\n  - With Launch On Startup on, recording and Replay work in them at a lower frame rate (about 22–27 frames a second on the top screen).\n  - Pressing HOME saves the recording, so HOME Menu gets the memory it needs. The recording goes on when you return to the game.\n  - Another game that crashes the same way within 30 s is added to /3ds/recorder/no_launcher.txt by itself. You can also add a title ID there.\n- Fixed: HOME Menu could crash after HOME in a game with Replay on when another plugin was also using memory. More memory is now kept free for HOME Menu.\n- Higher frame rate on an Old 3DS. The recorder measures which processor core encodes faster in each game and uses that one. Monster Hunter 4G went...\n\n----------\n\nv1.3.0 (2026-11-16)\nApplets no longer freeze the console, and a recording the recorder pauses by itself comes back as one video. Open Game Notes, the Friend List or the Internet Browser while recording: the recording steps aside and goes on afterwards. Close the lid and open it again: one recording, not several pieces.\n\nTested on an Old 3DS with Luma3DS 13.5. The applet handling has not been tried on a New 3DS yet: there the recording is saved when an applet opens and goes on (and is joined) when it closes. If something goes wrong, please open an issue and attach the log (phone page → Log for the developer, or /3ds/recorder/app.log and recorder.log from the SD card).\n\nWhat's new since 1.2.0\n\n- Fixed: opening an applet while recording froze it on its loading screen (#1). The recording is now saved and gives its memory back the moment an applet opens. On an Old 3DS it goes on next to a small applet at a lower frame rate; next to the Internet Browser nothing is recorded. After the applet the recording goes on as usual. Replay stops for the applet and starts again by itself.\n- One recording, not many. When the recorder pauses a recording by itself (an applet, the lid, HOME in a game that needs extra memory), the parts are joined into one recording in the background while the app is open. Keep the app open until Joining recordings is gone. A pause shows as half a second of the last picture; a recording you stopped yourself is never joined.\n- Lid: closing it saves the recording, opening it goes on wit...",
        "wiki": "https://github.com/BolgarMaxym97/3ds-recorder"
      }
    },
